{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3280","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3280","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3280\",\"parent_revision\":\"6cd340a78806e2583a8364fb469b5067769f6fcb0718016f2545aee7c37895d4\",\"root_revision\":\"6cd340a78806e2583a8364fb469b5067769f6fcb0718016f2545aee7c37895d4\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-28\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/analyze.md`'s Scope Sizing table assigns agents by scope tier: MINIMAL = fact-checker, groomer only; NARROW = impact-analyst, fact-checker, groomer only; STANDARD = impact-analyst, fact-checker, rtica-assessor, alignment-analyst, groomer; FULL = all 6 (adds classifier).\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/finalize.md`'s Output Validation Gate required-sections table unconditionally requires `Issue Classification` (contains `Type:` field) and `Design Intent Alignment` (contains an alignment verdict field) for every groomed item, with no scope-tier exception (the only documented exception is for the `Research` section).\\n\\n`Issue Classification` is produced only by the `classifier` agent, which the scope-sizing table includes only at FULL. `Design Intent Alignment` is produced only by `alignment-analyst`, included only at STANDARD and FULL. So any item groomed at MINIMAL or NARROW scope \u2014 the sizing the RT-ICA-driven flowchart in analyze.md would actually select for a simple defect with mostly-AVAILABLE conditions \u2014 can never pass the validation gate as written, because the agents that would produce two of the required sections were never spawned.\\n\\nObserved live: grooming #3276 (a P2 bug fix), the RT-ICA snapshot sized it NARROW (some DERIVABLE, zero MISSING, defect type). Proceeding at NARROW per the table would have left Issue Classification and Design Intent Alignment unwritten, guaranteed to fail the validation gate. The orchestrator manually escalated to FULL scope to route around this, reasoning it through in-session rather than following documented guidance \u2014 every future groom of a MINIMAL/NARROW-sized item will hit the identical dead end and have to make the same undocumented judgment call.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: possible directions for grooming to evaluate, not requirements \u2014 (1) make classifier and alignment-analyst part of every scope tier (effectively removing MINIMAL/NARROW as options, since finalize.md already requires their output), (2) make the required-sections table scope-conditional the same way the Research section already is, or (3) make Issue Classification/Design Intent Alignment orchestrator-writable fallbacks (like RT-ICA already is) when their owning agent wasn't spawned at the chosen scope.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 2026-08-29, while grooming #3276 via /dh:work-backlog-item\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-28\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"c457a0ee91c5b293828a5feca3099fd99a1fb7e69e7cc2a68cee929624883fca\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRSB_xw\"}"}